/-!
# The Picard sequence of a regular proper model is exact

Let `X ⟶ Spec(R)` be a regular proper model of a smooth projective curve `C` over the fraction
field of a discrete valuation ring with uniformizer `π`, with `H⁰(C, 𝒪_C) = K`, and let
`C₁, …, Cₙ` be the irreducible components of the special fibre `X_k`, with multiplicities `mᵢ`.
[Stacks, Tag 0C63] asserts that

`0 ⟶ ℤ ⟶ ℤ^{⊕n} ⟶ Pic(X) ⟶ Pic(C) ⟶ 0`

is exact, where the first map sends `1` to `(m₁, …, mₙ)`, the second sends the `i`th basis vector
to the class of `𝒪_X(Cᵢ)`, and the third is restriction to the generic fibre. This file proves
the three clauses of that exactness which `PicardSequence.lean` does not: exactness at `ℤ^{⊕n}`,
exactness at `Pic(X)`, and exactness at `Pic(C)`, and assembles the tag.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Models.surjective_genericFiberPicardRestriction` — exactness at `Pic(C)`.
* `Stacks.Models.genericFiberPicardRestriction_picardClass_specialFiberComponentIdeal` and
  `Stacks.Models.genericFiberPicardRestriction_componentPicardHom` — the component classes die
  on the generic fibre, which is the easy half of exactness at `Pic(X)`.
* `Stacks.Models.exact_componentPicardHom_genericFiberPicardRestriction` — exactness at `Pic(X)`.
* `Stacks.Models.componentProduct_injective` — the components are independent: an effective
  combination of them determines its exponents.
* `Stacks.Models.multiplicity_ne_zero` — every component occurs with positive multiplicity.
* `Stacks.Models.exact_multiplicityHom_componentPicardHom` — exactness at `ℤ^{⊕n}`.
* `Stacks.Models.picardSequence_exact` — **[Stacks, Tag 0C63]**, the whole sequence.

## Implementation notes

**Exactness at `Pic(C)`** is [Stacks, Tag 0BD9]: the generic fibre is an open subscheme of `X`
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Curves/Models/PicardSequenceGenericFibre.lean`), and every local
ring of the regular scheme `X` is a unique factorization domain, so an invertible module on the
generic fibre extends over the special fibre. The Picard-group bookkeeping is
`Stacks.Picard.pullbackClass_classOf` together with functoriality of the pullback of classes.

**Exactness at `Pic(X)`.** A class dying on `C` is the class of a module `ℒ` trivial on the
principal open `X_π`, which is the generic fibre. By
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isRegularSection_zeroScheme_disjoint_basicOpen` such an `ℒ` has a
nonzerodivisor global section vanishing nowhere on `X_π`, so its zero scheme is an effective
Cartier divisor supported in the special fibre; [Stacks, Tag 0BCP] writes that divisor as
`Σ aᵢ Cᵢ`, and the divisor's invertible sheaf reproduces `ℒ`. The converse half is the pullback
formula [Stacks, Tag 0C4U]: a component pulls back to the empty divisor on the generic fibre.

**Exactness at `ℤ^{⊕n}`.** Adding a large multiple of the multiplicity vector makes the
combination effective without changing its class, so it may be assumed effective; its invertible
sheaf is then trivial, hence it is the zero scheme of a global function, which lies in `R`
because `Γ(X, 𝒪_X) = R`
(`Stacks.Models.RegularProperModelSituation.isIso_globalSections_model`) and so is a unit times a
power of `π`. The combination is therefore that power of the special fibre, and the exponent
vectors agree by `Stacks.Models.componentProduct_injective`.

**How the components are compared.** The exponent of a component in an effective combination is
read off the stalk at the component's generic point: the other components do not pass through
that point, so their stalks there are the unit ideal, and the stalk of the combination is the
corresponding power of a principal ideal generated by a nonzero nonunit. This is also how
`Stacks.Models.multiplicity_ne_zero` is proved, and that positivity is what makes the shift above
possible.

**The index type.** `ℤ^{⊕n}` is `irreducibleComponents X_k → ℤ`; the components are finitely
many because `X_k` is a Noetherian scheme, and the resulting `Fintype` and the classical
`DecidableEq` are installed as local instances so that the statement of the tag needs no binder
beyond the situation of [Stacks, Tag 0C61].

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C63](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C63)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C61](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C61)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C5Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C5Z)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BD9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BD9)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BCP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BCP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C4U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C4U)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.Picard (ofScheme schemePullbackClass schemePullbackClassHom)

universe u

namespace Stacks.Models

variable (S : RegularProperModelSituation.{u})

/-! ### Surjectivity onto the Picard group of the generic fibre -/

/-- Pullback of classes along `f = e.hom ≫ g` is recovered from pullback along `g`, up to the
isomorphism `e`. -/
private theorem eq_schemePullbackClass_iff_of_iso_hom_comp {A B X : Scheme.{u}} (e : A ≅ B)
    (f : A ⟶ X) (g : B ⟶ X) (hfac : e.hom ≫ g = f) (x : ofScheme X) (y : ofScheme A) :
    y = Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClass f x ↔
      Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClass e.inv y = Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClass g x := by
  rw [← hfac, ← Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClass_comp]
  refine ⟨fun h => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
  · rw [h, Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClass_comp, e.inv_hom_id,
      Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClass_id]
  · rw [← h, Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClass_comp, e.hom_inv_id,
      Stacks.Picard.schemePullbackClass_id]

/-- **Every invertible module on the generic fibre extends to the model.** The generic fibre is
an open subscheme of `X`, every local ring of `X` is a unique factorization domain because `X` is
regular, and [Stacks, Tag 0BD9] extends an invertible module across such a complement. -/
theorem surjective_genericFiberPicardRestriction :
    Function.Surjective (genericFiberPicardRestriction S) := by
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian S.X := S.isLocallyNoetherian_X
  have : IsOpenImmersion S.toRegularModelSituation.genericFiberToModel :=
    S.toRegularModelSituation.isOpenImmersion_genericFiberToModel
  set j := S.toRegularModelSituation.genericFiberToModel
  set U : S.X.Opens := j.opensRange
  have hRange : Set.range j.base = Set.range U.ι.base := by
    rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    rfl
  let e : S.C ≅ U.toScheme := IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq j U.ι hRange
  intro y
  set L := Stacks.Picard.picardRepresentative S.C.toRingedSpace y
  have hLclass : Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass S.C.presheaf
      (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureIsSheaf S.C.toRingedSpace) L.obj L.property = y :=
    Stacks.Picard.classOf_picardRepresentative S.C.toRingedSpace y
  set LU : U.toScheme.Modules :=
    (Stacks.RingedSpace.pullbackFunctor e.inv.toLRSHom.toShHom).obj L.obj
  have hLU : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible U.toScheme.presheaf
      (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureIsSheaf U.toScheme.toRingedSpace) LU :=
    Stacks.RingedSpace.modulePullback_isInvertible_of e.inv.toLRSHom.toShHom L.obj L.property
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible U.toScheme.sheaf.obj
      U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf.property LU :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.toAlgebraicGeometry _ _ _ hLU
  obtain ⟨M, hM, ⟨iso⟩⟩ :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isInvertible_pullback_iso_of_isLocallyNoetherian U LU
      fun x _ => S.toRegularModelSituation.uniqueFactorizationMonoid_stalk x
  have hMinv : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.presheaf
      (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureIsSheaf S.X.toRingedSpace) M :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.ofAlgebraicGeometry _ _ _ hM
  refine ⟨Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass S.X.presheaf
    (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureIsSheaf S.X.toRingedSpace) M hMinv, ?_⟩
  have hstep : schemePullbackClass e.inv y =
      schemePullbackClass U.ι (Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass S.X.presheaf
        (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureIsSheaf S.X.toRingedSpace) M hMinv) := by
    rw [← hLclass]
    refine (Stacks.Picard.pullbackClass_classOf e.inv.toLRSHom.toShHom L.obj L.property).trans ?_
    refine Eq.trans ?_
      (Stacks.Picard.pullbackClass_classOf U.ι.toLRSHom.toShHom M hMinv).symm
    exact (Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_eq_iff _ _ _ _ _ _).2 ⟨iso⟩
  exact ((eq_schemePullbackClass_iff_of_iso_hom_comp e j U.ι
    (IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq_hom_fac j U.ι hRange) _ y).2 hstep).symm

/-! ### The component classes die on the generic fibre -/

/-- The support of a component of the special fibre is contained in that of the whole special
fibre. -/
private theorem supportSet_specialFiberComponentIdeal_subset_aux
    (Z : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber) :
    (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z).supportSet ⊆
      S.specialFiberIdeal.supportSet := by
  intro y hy
  have hy' : y ∈ ((S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z).support : Set S.X) := hy
  rw [S.toRegularModelSituation.coe_support_specialFiberComponentIdeal Z] at hy'
  obtain ⟨z, -, rfl⟩ := hy'
  change S.specialFiberι.base z ∈ (S.specialFiberIdeal.support : Set S.X)
  rw [S.toRegularModelSituation.coe_support_specialFiberIdeal]
  exact ⟨z, rfl⟩

/-- **A component of the special fibre pulls back to the empty divisor on the generic fibre**:
its support lies in the special fibre, which the generic fibre misses. -/
theorem comap_specialFiberComponentIdeal_genericFiberToModel
    (Z : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber) :
    (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z).comap
        S.toRegularModelSituation.genericFiberToModel = ⊤ := by
  refine (Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_eq_bot_iff _).mp ?_
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_comap]
  refine SetLike.coe_injective (Set.eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem.mpr fun c hc => ?_)
  exact S.toRegularModelSituation.notMem_supportSet_specialFiberIdeal c
    (supportSet_specialFiberComponentIdeal_subset_aux S Z hc)

/-- **The class of a component of the special fibre restricts to zero on the generic fibre**:
the component pulls back to the empty divisor, and `𝒪(D)` pulls back to `𝒪(f^{-1}D)` by
[Stacks, Tag 0C4U]. -/
theorem genericFiberPicardRestriction_picardClass_specialFiberComponentIdeal
    (Z : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber) :
    genericFiberPicardRestriction S
        (Stacks.Divisors.picardClass
          (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z)) = 0 := by
  set D := S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z
  set j := S.toRegularModelSituation.genericFiberToModel
  have hcomap : D.comap j = ⊤ := comap_specialFiberComponentIdeal_genericFiberToModel S Z
  have : Stacks.Divisors.IsPullbackDefined j D := by
    change Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (D.comap j)
    rw [hcomap]
    infer_instance
  change schemePullbackClass j (Stacks.Divisors.picardClass D) = 0
  refine (Stacks.Picard.pullbackClass_classOf j.toLRSHom.toShHom
    (Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf' D)
    (Stacks.Divisors.isInvertible_invertibleSheaf_picard D)).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_eq_iff _ _ _ _ _
    (Stacks.Divisors.isInvertible_invertibleSheaf_picard (D.comap j))).2
      ⟨Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheafPullbackIso j D⟩) ?_
  change Stacks.Divisors.picardClass (D.comap j) = 0
  rw [Stacks.Divisors.picardClass_congr hcomap]
  exact Stacks.Divisors.picardClass_top

/-- **Every integral combination of the component classes restricts to zero on the generic
fibre**, by additivity from the single components. -/
theorem genericFiberPicardRestriction_componentPicardHom
    [Fintype (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber)]
    (a : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber → ℤ) :
    genericFiberPicardRestriction S
        (componentPicardHom S
          (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal) a) = 0 := by
  rw [componentPicardHom_apply, map_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun Z _ => ?_
  rw [map_zsmul, genericFiberPicardRestriction_picardClass_specialFiberComponentIdeal S Z,
    smul_zero]

/-! ### Exactness at the Picard group of the model -/

/-- A finitely supported product of powers over a finite index type is the product over the whole
type: the omitted factors have exponent zero. -/
private theorem finsuppProd_eq_univProd {X : Scheme.{u}} {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]
    (D : ι → X.IdealSheafData) (a : ι →₀ ℕ) :
    (a.prod fun i n => D i ^ n) = ∏ i, D i ^ a i :=
  Finsupp.prod_fintype a _ fun _ => pow_zero _

/-- A class on the model that is trivial on the principal open `X_π` is the class of an
effective Cartier divisor whose support misses `X_π`. -/
private theorem exists_picardClass_eq_of_schemePullbackClass_basicOpen_eq_zero
    (x : ofScheme S.X)
    (hU0 : schemePullbackClass
      (S.X.basicOpen (S.toRegularModelSituation.uniformizerGlobalSection S.π)).ι x = 0) :
    ∃ (D : S.X.IdealSheafData) (_ : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D),
      (∀ y ∈ S.X.basicOpen (S.toRegularModelSituation.uniformizerGlobalSection S.π),
        y ∉ D.support) ∧ Stacks.Divisors.picardClass D = x := by
  have : IsIntegral S.X := S.toRegularModelSituation.isIntegral_X
  have : IsLocallyNoetherian S.X := S.isLocallyNoetherian_X
  have : CompactSpace S.X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace S.X_to_R
  have : IsNoetherian S.X := S.isNoetherian_X
  have : QuasiSeparatedSpace S.X := NoetherianSpace.to_quasiSeparatedSpace
  set g := S.toRegularModelSituation.uniformizerGlobalSection S.π
  set U : S.X.Opens := S.X.basicOpen g
  have hUne : (U : Set S.X).Nonempty := by
    rw [← (S.toRegularModelSituation.range_genericFiberToModel S.uniformizer :
      Set.range _ = (U : Set S.X))]
    exact Set.range_nonempty _
  set M := Stacks.Picard.picardRepresentative S.X.toRingedSpace x
  have hMx : Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass S.X.presheaf
      (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureIsSheaf S.X.toRingedSpace) M.obj M.property = x :=
    Stacks.Picard.classOf_picardRepresentative S.X.toRingedSpace x
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.sheaf.obj
      S.X.ringCatSheaf.property M.obj :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible.toAlgebraicGeometry _ _ _ M.property
  have htriv : Nonempty ((Scheme.Modules.pullback U.ι).obj M.obj ≅
      SheafOfModules.unit U.toScheme.ringCatSheaf) := by
    refine (Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_eq_zero_iff _ _ _
      (Stacks.RingedSpace.modulePullback_isInvertible_of U.ι.toLRSHom.toShHom M.obj
        M.property)).mp ?_
    rw [← Stacks.Picard.pullbackClass_classOf U.ι.toLRSHom.toShHom M.obj M.property, hMx]
    exact hU0
  obtain ⟨eU⟩ := AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_overIso_of_nonempty_pullbackIso U M.obj htriv
  obtain ⟨s, hsreg, hszero⟩ :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isRegularSection_zeroScheme_disjoint_basicOpen M.obj g hUne eU
  set D := AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme S.X M.obj (s.eval (Opposite.op ⊤))
  have hDeff : Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D :=
    (AlgebraicGeometry.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_zeroScheme_iff_isRegularSection
      S.X M.obj s).mpr hsreg
  exact ⟨D, hDeff, hszero, ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_eq_iff _ _ _ _ _ _).2
    ⟨(AlgebraicGeometry.invertibleSheafIsoZeroSchemeOfIsRegularSection
      M.obj s hsreg).symm⟩).trans hMx⟩

/-- **A class on the model that is trivial on the principal open `X_π` is a combination of the
components of the special fibre.** -/
private theorem mem_range_componentPicardHom_of_schemePullbackClass_basicOpen_eq_zero
    [Fintype (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber)] (x : ofScheme S.X)
    (hU0 : schemePullbackClass
      (S.X.basicOpen (S.toRegularModelSituation.uniformizerGlobalSection S.π)).ι x = 0) :
    x ∈ Set.range (componentPicardHom S S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal) := by
  classical
  have : IsNoetherian S.X := S.isNoetherian_X
  obtain ⟨D, hDeff, hD, hclass⟩ :=
    exists_picardClass_eq_of_schemePullbackClass_basicOpen_eq_zero S x hU0
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := AlgebraicGeometry.exists_finsupp_eq_prod_of_support_cover D hDeff
    S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal
    (fun Z => ⟨inferInstance, S.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_specialFiberComponent Z⟩)
    fun y hy => by
      refine S.exists_mem_supportSet_specialFiberComponentIdeal ?_
      change y ∈ (S.specialFiberIdeal.support : Set S.X)
      rw [S.toRegularModelSituation.coe_support_specialFiberIdeal_eq_compl_basicOpen S.uniformizer]
      exact fun hyU => hD y hyU hy
  refine ⟨fun Z => (a Z : ℤ), ?_⟩
  rw [componentPicardHom_apply, ← hclass, Stacks.Divisors.picardClass_congr
    (ha.trans (finsuppProd_eq_univProd _ a)), Stacks.Divisors.picardClass_prod_pow]

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0C63, exactness at `Pic(X)`.** An invertible module on the model whose
restriction to the generic fibre is trivial is `𝒪_X(Σ aᵢ Cᵢ)` for integers `aᵢ`, and conversely
every such combination restricts to zero.

The generic fibre is the principal open `X_π`, so a class dying there is the class of a module
trivial on `X_π`; that module has a nonzerodivisor global section vanishing nowhere on `X_π`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isRegularSection_zeroScheme_disjoint_basicOpen`), whose zero scheme is
therefore an effective Cartier divisor supported in the special fibre, and [Stacks, Tag 0BCP]
writes that divisor as a nonnegative combination of the components. -/
theorem exact_componentPicardHom_genericFiberPicardRestriction
    [Fintype (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber)] :
    Function.Exact
      (componentPicardHom S S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal)
      (genericFiberPicardRestriction S) := by
  have : IsOpenImmersion S.toRegularModelSituation.genericFiberToModel :=
    S.toRegularModelSituation.isOpenImmersion_genericFiberToModel
  set j := S.toRegularModelSituation.genericFiberToModel
  set U : S.X.Opens :=
    S.X.basicOpen (S.toRegularModelSituation.uniformizerGlobalSection S.π)
  have hRange : Set.range j.base = Set.range U.ι.base := by
    rw [Scheme.Opens.range_ι]
    exact S.toRegularModelSituation.range_genericFiberToModel S.uniformizer
  let e : S.C ≅ U.toScheme := IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq j U.ι hRange
  refine fun x => ⟨fun hx => ?_, ?_⟩
  · refine mem_range_componentPicardHom_of_schemePullbackClass_basicOpen_eq_zero S x ?_
    exact ((eq_schemePullbackClass_iff_of_iso_hom_comp e j U.ι
      (IsOpenImmersion.isoOfRangeEq_hom_fac j U.ι hRange) x 0).1 hx.symm).symm.trans
        (Stacks.Picard.pullbackClassHom e.inv.toLRSHom.toShHom).map_zero
  · rintro ⟨a, rfl⟩
    exact genericFiberPicardRestriction_componentPicardHom S a

/-! ### The generic points of the components, and the stalks there -/

/-- **The generic point of a component of the special fibre**, as a point of the model: the
image of the generic point of the integral closed subscheme cut out by the component. -/
abbrev componentGenericPoint (Z : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber) : S.X :=
  (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z).subschemeι.base
    (genericPoint (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z).subscheme)

/-- **The support of a component of the special fibre is contained in that of the whole special
fibre.** -/
theorem supportSet_specialFiberComponentIdeal_subset
    (Z : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber) :
    (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z).supportSet ⊆
      S.specialFiberIdeal.supportSet :=
  supportSet_specialFiberComponentIdeal_subset_aux S Z

/-- **The generic point of one component lies on another only when the two coincide**: the
closure of the point is the whole component, and two irreducible components one of which contains
the other are equal. -/
theorem mem_supportSet_specialFiberComponentIdeal_iff
    (Z W : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber) :
    componentGenericPoint S Z ∈
        (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal W).supportSet ↔ Z = W := by
  refine ⟨fun h => ?_, ?_⟩
  · have h' : componentGenericPoint S Z ∈
        ((S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal W).support : Set S.X) := h
    rw [S.toRegularModelSituation.coe_support_specialFiberComponentIdeal W] at h'
    have hsub : S.specialFiberι.base '' (Z.1 : Set S.specialFiber) ⊆
        S.specialFiberι.base '' (W.1 : Set S.specialFiber) := by
      rw [← S.toRegularModelSituation.closure_singleton_genericPoint_specialFiberComponent Z]
      exact closure_minimal (Set.singleton_subset_iff.mpr h')
        (S.toRegularModelSituation.isClosed_image_specialFiberComponent W)
    exact Subtype.ext (Z.2.eq_of_subset W.2.1
      ((Set.image_subset_image_iff S.specialFiberι.isClosedEmbedding.injective).mp hsub))
  · rintro rfl
    change componentGenericPoint S Z ∈
      ((S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z).support : Set S.X)
    rw [S.toRegularModelSituation.coe_support_specialFiberComponentIdeal Z,
      ← S.toRegularModelSituation.closure_singleton_genericPoint_specialFiberComponent Z]
    exact subset_closure (Set.mem_singleton _)

/-- Taking the stalk of an ideal sheaf at a point is multiplicative. -/
private def stalkMonoidHom (X : Scheme.{u}) (x : X) :
    X.IdealSheafData →* Ideal (X.presheaf.stalk x) where
  toFun I := AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk I x
  map_one' := by
    have h : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk (1 : X.IdealSheafData) x = ⊤ := by
      refine (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_not_mem_support _ x).mpr ?_
      rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.one_eq_top, Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_top]
      exact id
    rw [h, Ideal.one_eq_top]
  map_mul' I J := AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_mul I J x

/-- **The stalk of a combination of the components at the generic point of one of them is the
power of that component's stalk**: the other components do not pass through the point, so their
stalks there are the unit ideal. -/
theorem stalk_componentProduct [Fintype (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber)]
    (Z : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber)
    (k : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber → ℕ) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
        (∏ W, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal W ^ k W)
        (componentGenericPoint S Z) =
      AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
        (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z)
        (componentGenericPoint S Z) ^ k Z := by
  have hprod : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
      (∏ W, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal W ^ k W)
      (componentGenericPoint S Z) =
      ∏ W, AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
        (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal W)
        (componentGenericPoint S Z) ^ k W := by
    change stalkMonoidHom S.X (componentGenericPoint S Z)
      (∏ W, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal W ^ k W) = _
    rw [map_prod]
    exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun W _ =>
      map_pow (stalkMonoidHom S.X (componentGenericPoint S Z)) _ (k W)
  rw [hprod]
  refine Finset.prod_eq_single_of_mem Z (Finset.mem_univ Z) fun W _ hW => ?_
  rw [(AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_not_mem_support _ _).mpr
      (fun hc => hW ((mem_supportSet_specialFiberComponentIdeal_iff S Z W).mp hc).symm),
    ← Ideal.one_eq_top, one_pow]

/-- **The stalk of a component at its own generic point is generated by a single element that is
neither zero nor a unit.** The component is an effective Cartier divisor, so on an affine chart
its ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor; the germ of that generator is nonzero because the
model is integral, and is not a unit because the point lies on the component. -/
theorem exists_stalk_specialFiberComponentIdeal_eq_span
    (Z : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber) :
    ∃ f : S.X.presheaf.stalk (componentGenericPoint S Z),
      AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
          (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z)
          (componentGenericPoint S Z) = Ideal.span {f} ∧ f ≠ 0 ∧ ¬ IsUnit f := by
  have : IsIntegral S.X := S.toRegularModelSituation.isIntegral_X
  have hx : componentGenericPoint S Z ∈
      (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z).supportSet :=
    (mem_supportSet_specialFiberComponentIdeal_iff S Z Z).mpr rfl
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, c, hc, ec, hec⟩ :=
    (Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_iff_affineLocal
        (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z)).mp
      (S.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_specialFiberComponent Z) _ hx
  have hgen : (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z).ideal ⟨V, hV⟩ =
      Ideal.span {c} :=
    Stacks.Divisors.ideal_eq_quotient_of_chart _ V hV (Ideal.span {c}) ec hec
  have hstalk : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
      (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z)
      (componentGenericPoint S Z) =
      Ideal.span {S.X.presheaf.germ V (componentGenericPoint S Z) hxV c} := by
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ _ _ ⟨V, hV⟩ hxV, hgen, Ideal.map_span,
      Set.image_singleton]
  refine ⟨S.X.presheaf.germ V (componentGenericPoint S Z) hxV c, hstalk, ?_, ?_⟩
  · have : Nonempty V := ⟨⟨componentGenericPoint S Z, hxV⟩⟩
    have : Nontrivial Γ(S.X, V) := Scheme.component_nontrivial S.X V
    have hc0 : c ≠ 0 := fun h0 => (one_ne_zero (α := Γ(S.X, V))) (hc.left (by simp [h0]))
    exact fun h0 => hc0 (germ_injective_of_isIntegral S.X (componentGenericPoint S Z) hxV
      (h0.trans (map_zero _).symm))
  · exact fun hu => (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_not_mem_support
      (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z)
      (componentGenericPoint S Z)).mp (by rwa [hstalk, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_top]) hx

/-- In a domain, the powers of the ideal generated by a nonzero nonunit are pairwise
distinct. -/
private theorem span_singleton_pow_injective {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsDomain A]
    {f : A} (hf : f ≠ 0) (hu : ¬ IsUnit f) :
    Function.Injective fun n : ℕ => (Ideal.span {f} : Ideal A) ^ n := by
  suffices h : ∀ p q : ℕ, (Ideal.span {f} : Ideal A) ^ p =
      (Ideal.span {f} : Ideal A) ^ q → ¬ p < q by
    intro p q hpq
    exact Nat.le_antisymm (Nat.le_of_not_gt (h q p hpq.symm)) (Nat.le_of_not_gt (h p q hpq))
  intro p q hpq hlt
  obtain ⟨d, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_lt hlt
  have hmem : f ^ p ∈ (Ideal.span {f} : Ideal A) ^ (p + d + 1) := by
    rw [← hpq, Ideal.span_singleton_pow]
    exact Ideal.subset_span (by simp)
  rw [Ideal.span_singleton_pow, Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at hmem
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hmem
  have he : 1 = f ^ (d + 1) * b := by
    refine mul_left_cancel₀ (pow_ne_zero p hf) ?_
    simpa only [mul_one, ← Nat.add_assoc, pow_add, mul_assoc] using hb
  exact hu (isUnit_pow_succ_iff.mp (IsUnit.of_mul_eq_one b he.symm))

/-- **The map sending an exponent vector to the corresponding combination of the components of
the special fibre is injective.** The exponent at a component is recovered from the stalk at its
generic point, where every other component contributes the unit ideal. -/
theorem componentProduct_injective [Fintype (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber)] :
    Function.Injective fun k : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber → ℕ =>
      ∏ Z, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z ^ k Z := by
  have : IsIntegral S.X := S.toRegularModelSituation.isIntegral_X
  intro k k' h
  funext Z
  obtain ⟨f, hstalk, hf0, hfu⟩ := exists_stalk_specialFiberComponentIdeal_eq_span S Z
  have hk := congrArg (fun I : S.X.IdealSheafData =>
    AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk I (componentGenericPoint S Z)) h
  rw [stalk_componentProduct S Z k, stalk_componentProduct S Z k', hstalk] at hk
  exact span_singleton_pow_injective hf0 hfu hk

/-- **Every component of the special fibre occurs in the decomposition with positive
multiplicity.** If one had multiplicity zero, the stalk of the special fibre at its generic point
would be the unit ideal, and the point would lie off the special fibre. -/
theorem multiplicity_ne_zero [Fintype (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber)]
    (m : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber → ℕ)
    (hdec : S.specialFiberIdeal =
      ∏ Z, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z ^ m Z)
    (Z : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber) : m Z ≠ 0 := by
  intro h0
  have hx : componentGenericPoint S Z ∈ S.specialFiberIdeal.supportSet :=
    supportSet_specialFiberComponentIdeal_subset S Z
      ((mem_supportSet_specialFiberComponentIdeal_iff S Z Z).mpr rfl)
  have htop : AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk S.specialFiberIdeal
      (componentGenericPoint S Z) = ⊤ := by
    rw [hdec, stalk_componentProduct S Z m, h0, pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top]
  exact ((AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_top_iff_not_mem_support _ _).mp htop) hx

/-- **An integer vector becomes nonnegative after adding a large multiple of the multiplicity
vector**, the multiplicities being at least one. -/
theorem exists_nat_shift_nonneg [Finite (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber)]
    (m : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber → ℕ) (hm : ∀ Z, m Z ≠ 0)
    (a : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber → ℤ) :
    ∃ n : ℕ, ∀ Z, 0 ≤ a Z + (n : ℤ) * (m Z : ℤ) := by
  classical
  have := Fintype.ofFinite (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber)
  set N := Finset.univ.sup fun W => (a W).natAbs
  refine ⟨N, fun Z => ?_⟩
  have h1 : (a Z).natAbs ≤ N := Finset.le_sup (f := fun W => (a W).natAbs) (Finset.mem_univ Z)
  have hb : -(N : ℤ) ≤ a Z := by omega
  have h2 : (1 : ℤ) ≤ (m Z : ℤ) := by exact_mod_cast Nat.one_le_iff_ne_zero.mpr (hm Z)
  have hmul : (N : ℤ) ≤ (N : ℤ) * (m Z : ℤ) := le_mul_of_one_le_right (Int.natCast_nonneg _) h2
  linarith

/-! ### Exactness at the free abelian group on the components -/

/-- **An ideal sheaf generated on every affine open by one nonzero element of `R` is a power of
the special fibre.** -/
private theorem exists_eq_specialFiberIdeal_pow_of_ideal_eq_span_chartHom
    (E : S.X.IdealSheafData) {r : S.R} (hr0 : r ≠ 0)
    (hE : ∀ (V : S.X.Opens) (hV : IsAffineOpen V),
      E.ideal ⟨V, hV⟩ = Ideal.span {(chartHom S.X_to_R V).hom r}) :
    ∃ l : ℕ, E = S.specialFiberIdeal ^ l := by
  obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.associated_pow_irreducible hr0 S.uniformizer
  refine ⟨l, Scheme.IdealSheafData.ext ?_⟩
  funext V
  obtain ⟨V, hV⟩ := V
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.ideal_pow, Pi.pow_apply, hE V hV,
    Stacks.Models.specialFiberIdeal_ideal_eq_span (k := S.k) S.residueEquiv S.X_to_R
      S.uniformizer V hV,
    Ideal.span_singleton_pow]
  have hassoc : Associated ((chartHom S.X_to_R V).hom r)
      ((chartHom S.X_to_R V).hom (S.π ^ l)) := hl.map (chartHom S.X_to_R V).hom
  rw [map_pow] at hassoc
  exact le_antisymm (Ideal.span_singleton_le_span_singleton.mpr hassoc.symm.dvd)
    (Ideal.span_singleton_le_span_singleton.mpr hassoc.dvd)

/-- **An effective Cartier divisor on an integral scheme has nonzero ideal on every affine open
containing the generic point.** -/
private theorem ideal_ne_bot_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_genericPoint_mem {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsIntegral X] (E : X.IdealSheafData) [Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor E]
    (V : X.affineOpens) (hV : genericPoint X ∈ V.1) : E.ideal V ≠ ⊥ := by
  intro hid
  refine AlgebraicGeometry.genericPoint_notMem_supportSet_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor
    (D := E) inferInstance ?_
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_supportSet_iff_of_mem (U := V) hV, hid]
  refine (Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff X _ _).mpr fun c hc => ?_
  rw [Ideal.mem_bot.mp hc, Scheme.basicOpen_zero]
  simp

/-- **An effective Cartier divisor on the model with trivial invertible sheaf is a power of the
special fibre.** -/
private theorem exists_eq_specialFiberIdeal_pow_of_picardClass_eq_zero (E : S.X.IdealSheafData)
    [Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor E] (hE : Stacks.Divisors.picardClass E = 0) :
    ∃ l : ℕ, E = S.specialFiberIdeal ^ l := by
  have : IsIntegral S.X := S.toRegularModelSituation.isIntegral_X
  obtain ⟨ε⟩ := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.picardClass_eq_zero_iff S.X.presheaf
    (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureIsSheaf S.X.toRingedSpace) (Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf' E)
    (Stacks.Divisors.isInvertible_invertibleSheaf_picard E)).mp hE
  set L₀ : S.X.Modules := SheafOfModules.unit S.X.ringCatSheaf
  have : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible S.X.sheaf.obj
      S.X.ringCatSheaf.property L₀ := Stacks.Models.isInvertible_unit S.X
  have ε' : Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheaf' E ≅ L₀ := ε
  have hchartIso : IsIso (chartHom S.X_to_R (⊤ : S.X.Opens)) := by
    rw [S.toRegularModelSituation.chartHom_top]
    exact S.isIso_globalSections_model
  set t : Γ(L₀, (⊤ : S.X.Opens)) :=
    Scheme.Modules.Hom.app ε'.hom ⊤ (Stacks.Divisors.divisorSheafGlobalSection E)
  have hZt : AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme S.X L₀ t = E :=
    (AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_eq_of_iso ε' rfl).symm.trans
      (Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_canonicalSection E)
  have hidealZ : ∀ (V : S.X.Opens) (hV : IsAffineOpen V),
      E.ideal ⟨V, hV⟩ =
        Ideal.span {S.X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : V ≤ ⊤)).op t} := by
    intro V hV
    rw [← hZt]
    exact AlgebraicGeometry.zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization S.X L₀ t ⟨V, hV⟩
      (LinearEquiv.refl _ _) _ rfl
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
    (chartHom S.X_to_R (⊤ : S.X.Opens))).2 t
  have hrestr : ∀ (V : S.X.Opens),
      S.X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : V ≤ ⊤)).op t = (chartHom S.X_to_R V).hom r := by
    intro V
    rw [← hr]
    exact congrArg (fun φ : CommRingCat.of S.R ⟶ Γ(S.X, V) => φ.hom r)
      (chartHom_comp_map S.X_to_R (homOfLE (le_top : V ≤ ⊤)).op)
  have ht0 : t ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    obtain ⟨-, ⟨V₀, hV₀, rfl⟩, hgV₀, -⟩ :=
      S.X.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open
        (Set.mem_univ (genericPoint S.X)) isOpen_univ
    refine ideal_ne_bot_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_genericPoint_mem E ⟨V₀, hV₀⟩ hgV₀ ?_
    rw [hidealZ V₀ hV₀, h0]
    exact Ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot.mpr (map_zero _)
  have hr0 : r ≠ 0 := fun h0 => ht0 (by rw [← hr, h0]; exact map_zero _)
  exact exists_eq_specialFiberIdeal_pow_of_ideal_eq_span_chartHom S E hr0 fun V hV => by
    rw [hidealZ V hV, hrestr V]

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0C63, exactness at `ℤ^{⊕n}`.** A combination `Σ aᵢ Cᵢ` of the
components of the special fibre has trivial invertible sheaf exactly when `a` is an integral
multiple of the multiplicity vector.

After adding a large multiple of the multiplicity vector the combination becomes effective, and
its invertible sheaf is still trivial; so it is the zero scheme of a global function, which lies
in `R` because `Γ(X, 𝒪_X) = R`, hence is a unit times a power of the uniformizer; so the
combination is that power of the special fibre, and the exponent vectors agree because the
components are independent. -/
theorem exact_multiplicityHom_componentPicardHom
    [Fintype (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber)]
    (m : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber → ℕ)
    (hdec : S.specialFiberIdeal =
      ∏ Z, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z ^ m Z) :
    Function.Exact (multiplicityHom m)
      (componentPicardHom S S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal) := by
  have : IsIntegral S.X := S.toRegularModelSituation.isIntegral_X
  refine fun a => ⟨fun ha => ?_, ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := exists_nat_shift_nonneg S m (multiplicity_ne_zero S m hdec) a
    set k : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber → ℕ :=
      fun Z => (a Z + (n : ℤ) * (m Z : ℤ)).toNat
    have hk : ∀ Z, (k Z : ℤ) = a Z + (n : ℤ) * (m Z : ℤ) :=
      fun Z => Int.toNat_of_nonneg (hn Z)
    set E : S.X.IdealSheafData :=
      ∏ Z, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z ^ k Z
    have hEclass : Stacks.Divisors.picardClass E = 0 := by
      have h1 : Stacks.Divisors.picardClass E =
          componentPicardHom S S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal
            (fun Z => (k Z : ℤ)) := by
        rw [componentPicardHom_apply]
        exact Stacks.Divisors.picardClass_prod_pow Finset.univ
          S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal k
      have h2 : (fun Z => ((k Z : ℕ) : ℤ)) = a + multiplicityHom m (n : ℤ) := funext hk
      rw [h1, h2, map_add, ha,
        componentPicardHom_multiplicityHom S
          S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal m hdec, add_zero]
    obtain ⟨l, hEspec⟩ := exists_eq_specialFiberIdeal_pow_of_picardClass_eq_zero S E hEclass
    have hprodeq : (∏ Z, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z ^ k Z) =
        ∏ Z, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z ^ (m Z * l) :=
      hEspec.trans (by rw [hdec, ← Finset.prod_pow]; simp_rw [pow_mul])
    refine ⟨(l : ℤ) - (n : ℤ), ?_⟩
    funext Z
    have hcast : a Z + (n : ℤ) * (m Z : ℤ) = (m Z : ℤ) * (l : ℤ) := by
      rw [← hk Z, congrFun (componentProduct_injective S hprodeq) Z]
      push_cast
      ring
    change ((l : ℤ) - (n : ℤ)) * (m Z : ℤ) = a Z
    linarith
  · rintro ⟨c, rfl⟩
    exact componentPicardHom_multiplicityHom S
      S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal m hdec c

/-! ### The Picard sequence of a regular proper model -/

/-- The components of the special fibre of a regular proper model form a finite set, so the free
abelian group on them is `ℤ^{⊕n}`. Local, because it is the canonical finiteness structure only
up to the irrelevant choice of an enumeration. -/
noncomputable local instance fintypeIrreducibleComponentsSpecialFiber
    (S : RegularProperModelSituation.{u}) : Fintype (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber) :=
  @Fintype.ofFinite _ S.finite_irreducibleComponents_specialFiber.to_subtype

/-- Equality of components of the special fibre is decided classically. -/
local instance decidableEqIrreducibleComponentsSpecialFiber
    (S : RegularProperModelSituation.{u}) :
    DecidableEq (irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber) := Classical.decEq _

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0C63.** In Situation 0C61 there is an exact sequence

`0 ⟶ ℤ ⟶ ℤ^{⊕n} ⟶ Pic(X) ⟶ Pic(C) ⟶ 0`

where the first map sends `1` to the vector `(m₁, …, mₙ)` of multiplicities of the irreducible
components `C₁, …, Cₙ` of the special fibre, and the second map sends the `i`th basis vector to
the class of `𝒪_X(Cᵢ)`.

The three maps are the group homomorphisms `Stacks.Models.multiplicityHom`,
`Stacks.Models.componentPicardHom` and `Stacks.Models.genericFiberPicardRestriction`, the last
being pullback of Picard classes along the inclusion of the generic fibre; the components are the
irreducible components of `X_k` with their reduced induced structure, which are effective Cartier
divisors by [Stacks, Tag 0C5Z]; and `ℤ^{⊕n}` is the group of integer families on them, the
components being finitely many. The decomposition `X_k = Σ mᵢ Cᵢ` with which the situation opens
is part of the conclusion, and the seven conjuncts are, in order: that decomposition, the value
of the first map on `1`, the values of the second map on the basis vectors, exactness at `ℤ`
(injectivity of the first map), exactness at `ℤ^{⊕n}`, exactness at `Pic(X)`, and exactness at
`Pic(C)` (surjectivity of the third map). -/
@[stacks 0C63, ega "IV 21.6.11" "special case", sga "6 X 7.8" "partial, special case"]
theorem picardSequence_exact (S : RegularProperModelSituation.{u}) :
    ∃ m : irreducibleComponents S.specialFiber → ℕ,
      S.specialFiberIdeal =
          ∏ Z, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z ^ m Z ∧
        multiplicityHom m 1 = (fun Z => (m Z : ℤ)) ∧
        (∀ Z, componentPicardHom S S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal
            (Pi.single Z 1) =
          Stacks.Divisors.picardClass
            (S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z)) ∧
        Function.Injective (multiplicityHom m) ∧
        Function.Exact (multiplicityHom m)
            (componentPicardHom S S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal) ∧
        Function.Exact
            (componentPicardHom S S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal)
            (genericFiberPicardRestriction S) ∧
        Function.Surjective (genericFiberPicardRestriction S) := by
  obtain ⟨mf, hdecf⟩ := S.exists_specialFiberIdeal_eq_prod
  have hdec : S.specialFiberIdeal =
      ∏ Z, S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal Z ^ mf Z :=
    hdecf.trans (finsuppProd_eq_univProd
      S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal mf)
  refine ⟨⇑mf, hdec, multiplicityHom_one ⇑mf, fun Z => componentPicardHom_single S _ Z,
    injective_multiplicityHom S S.toRegularModelSituation.specialFiberComponentIdeal ⇑mf hdec,
    exact_multiplicityHom_componentPicardHom S ⇑mf hdec,
    exact_componentPicardHom_genericFiberPicardRestriction S,
    surjective_genericFiberPicardRestriction S⟩

end Stacks.Models

